$$
\vec{a} = 2\hat{i} + \hat{j} - \hat{k}, \vec{b} = ((\vec{a} \times (\hat{i} + \hat{j})) \times \hat{i}) \times \hat{i}
$$

$$
\vec{a} \times (\hat{i} + \hat{j}) = \begin{vmatrix} \hat{i} & \hat{j} & \hat{k} \\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\ 1 & 1 & 0 \end{vmatrix} = \hat{i} - \hat{j} + \hat{k}
$$

$$
(\vec{a} \times (\hat{i} + \hat{j})) \times \hat{i} = \hat{k} + \hat{j}
$$

$$
((\vec{a} \times (\hat{i} + \hat{j})) \times \hat{i}) \times \hat{i} = (\hat{k} + \hat{j}) \times \hat{i} = \hat{j} - \hat{k}
$$

$$
\text{Projection of } \vec{a} \text{ on } \vec{b} = \frac{\vec{a} \cdot \vec{b}}{|\vec{b}|} = \frac{(2\hat{i} + \hat{j} - \hat{k}) \cdot (\hat{i} - \hat{k})}{|\hat{i} - \hat{k}|} = \frac{1+1}{\sqrt{2}} = \sqrt{2}
$$

Square of projection of \(\vec{a}\) or \(\vec{b}\) is 2

